Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every individual test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

*(You can also use a constructor / `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` if you prefer.)*

---

### 2. Once before the first / after the last test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before any test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after all tests in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Can_Place_Order() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Class-level hooks must be **static**.

---

### 3. Once per assembly (before any / after all tests in the assembly)

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once per entire test session (start → end of the whole run)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick-reference table

| Scope | Before | After |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` (static) | `[After(Class)]` (static) |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` (static) | `[After(Assembly)]` (static) |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` (static) | `[After(TestSession)]` (static) |

**Bonus:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (and `Class`/`Assembly` variants) are *global* cross-cutting hooks that fire for every test regardless of which class they live in—handy for logging or diagnostics. All hooks optionally accept a context parameter and/or `CancellationToken`.
